      "writtenOn": "2023-01-31T21:51:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If it helps simplify the implementation, we\u0027ve had some discussions about requiring all backend textures that would be wrapped in an SkSurface be both renderable and texturable. If we only have one capability, we either have to go through these sorts of workarounds for copies or we\u0027re unable to read back from the texture for complex blending scenarios, which impacts correctness.\n\nWe can easily update our own apps to ensure the swapchain resources are configured correctly for this context. Clients that want to create swapchains that are framebuffer-only could do so, but would have to then manually or copy a separate offscreen SkSurface into the framebuffer for each frame. Like you pointed out in another comment, in practice, I don\u0027t think this would actually impact Chrome very much.",
